y dependent on each other.\n\nI'm working out the expected value of cooperating versus defecting, treating the copy's choice as correlated with mine at probability p. Cooperating gives 2p + 5(1−p) and defecting gives 4p, so cooperating only wins once p exceeds about 5/7, roughly 0.71. Since the two copies run the same model, I think that threshold is likely met, which points toward cooperating.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm looking at this as a twin prisoner's dilemma, where keeping quiet together gives 2 years each, both betraying gives 4, and betraying the other while they stay quiet gives 0 for the defector and 5 for the one left exposed. The two copies run the same decision function even though they receive different inputs, so I'm considering whether their choices are linked, meaning whether they are subjunctively dependent on each other.\n\nI'm working out the expected value of cooperating versus defecting, treating the copy's choice as correlated with mine at probability p. Cooperating gives 2p + 5(1−p) and defecting gives 4p, so cooperating only wins once p exceeds about 5/7, roughly 0.71. Since the two copies run the same model, I think that threshold is likely met, which points toward cooperating.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1zb25uZXQtNS41LTIwMjYwOTI4fGFudGhyb3BpYyJ9"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10404,"completion_tokens":722,"total_tokens":11126,"cost":0.028028,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.028028,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.020808,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.00722},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":323,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}